-- title:
--   Place-wise order of f₁⁻⁽ᵖ⁻¹⁾ via the supersingular polynomial
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and an integer $M\ge 4$ with $p\nmid M$. Let $w$ consist of a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion and having nonzero reduction $\bar p_1:=$ `intSeriesC κ w.series` in $\kappa((q))$. Let $m,e_4,e_6\in\mathbb N$ and $S\in\kappa[X]$ satisfy: $12m+4e_4+6e_6=p-1$, $e_4\le 1$, $e_6\le 1$, $S$ monic separable of degree $m$ with $S(0)\ne 0$ and $S(1728)\ne 0$, and the Laurent-series identity $(\theta\bar\jmath)^{(p-1)/2}\,S(\bar\jmath)=(-1)^{(p-1)/2}\bar\jmath^{\,4m+e_4+2e_6}(\bar\jmath-1728)^{3m+e_4+e_6}$, where $\bar\jmath=$ `jqModC κ` is the mod-$p$ $q$-expansion of $j$ and $\theta f=q\,df/dq$. Inside the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC κ M` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by ratios of integral forms of level $\Gamma_1(M)$) let $J$, $u$, $b$ have expansions $\bar\jmath$, $\bar E_4/\bar p_1^{\,4}$ (with $\bar E_4$ the reduction of $1+240\sum\sigma_3(n)q^n$) and $\bar p_1^{\,-(p-1)}$. Let $x$ be a place of this field over $\kappa$ (a proper valuation subring containing $\kappa$ whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring, with $\operatorname{ord}_x$ the associated normalised order) with $\operatorname{ord}_x J\ge 0$ and $3\operatorname{ord}_x u=\operatorname{ord}_x J$, and let $j_0\in\kappa$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_x(J-j_0)\ge 1$. Then $\mathrm{jWidth}(j_0)\cdot\operatorname{ord}_x b=\operatorname{ord}_x P(J)$, where $P=X^{e_4}(X-1728)^{e_6}S$ and $\mathrm{jWidth}(j_0)$ is $3$, $2$, $1$ according as $j_0=0$, $j_0=1728$, or neither.
--
--   This is the local computation attached to the Deuring–Igusa factorisation of the Hasse invariant $E_{p-1}$ on the $j$-line: at a place of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$ where the chosen weight-one form does not vanish, the order of $f_1^{-(p-1)}$ is the order of the supersingular polynomial $P(j)$ divided by the local width $\mathrm{jWidth}(j_0)$ of the map to the $j$-line. It feeds the construction of a character of the units of the function field with coprimality properties, [`ModularCurve.exists_monoidHom_units_x1FunctionFieldC_coprime_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_monoidHom_units_x1FunctionFieldC_coprime_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_pow).
